*9/16/86 merge in Mike Borkowski's mods UW002,UW003              [1.24]
*[1.20] Add hook for local BROWN adparse pre-proc routine.
*[1.19] Allow quoted-string == atom for user name
*[1.15] Mistake with checking for "AT"
ADP      TITLE 'CUCCA VM NETWORK MAILER VERSION 1 - PARSE AN ARPA-STYLE*
                MAIL ADDRESS'
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
*      MAILER -- Copyright (c) 1982,1986 Columbia University.         *
*    Program Property of the Trustees of Columbia University in the   *
*    City of New York.                                                *
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
* This routine will parse an in-core address list according to
* a subset of the arpa message format standard described in
* RFC #733.
* E. ALAN CROSSWELL                       CUCCA     7/81
*
* LAST EDIT: 11/16/82 BY ALAN CROSSWELL
*
* ON ENTRY, R1 POINTS TO A PARMLIST:
PAB      DSECT ,
@STR     DS    A             ADDRESS OF INPUT STRING POINTER
@END     DS    A             ADDRESS OF END OF STRING POINTER
@STK     DS    A             ADDRESS OF STACK POINTER
@LEN     DS    F             ADDRESS OF STACK LENGTH
@TOK     DS    A             ADDRESS OF TOKEN LIST POINTER (OUTPUT)
@PAR     DS    A             ADDRESS OF PARSE LIST POINTER (OUTPUT)
         SPACE ,
* ON RETURN, THE WORK BUFFER(STACK) POINTER AND LENGTH ARE UPDATED
* TO POINT TO THE NEXT UNUSED BYTE AND THE ADDRESSES OF THE TOKEN
* LIST AND PARSE LIST ARE RETURNED.
*
* Interpretation of token list -
*  The token list consists of a singly linked list of tokens in the
*  order that they appear in the input string. Each token is
*  described by a "TOKEND" dsect which tells the token type, the
*  address of the next token and the address and length of the
*  actual string that the token represents.
*
* Interpretation of the parse list:
*  the parse list consists of a list of representations of
*  individual addresses in an address list.  each MBOX dsect
*  describes one full address which consists of a user name and
*  list of one or more host names (i.e. FOO@BAR@BAZ).  the
*  MBOX contains a pointer to the next address in the list,
*  a pointer to the list of tokens in the user name and a count
*  of how many tokens are in it (usually only 1) and a pointer
*  to a list of host names and the count of how many names are
*  present.  The NODE dsect is used to represent the tokens
*  in a user name or host name list. Each NODE points to the
*  next NODE for the same item (if any) and down to the
*  token descriptor that represents that particular token.
*
*  Why it's so complicated looking:
*   The use of 3 levels of pointers makes manipulation and editing
*   of any given address easy to do. As an example, the following
*   address string may be supplied:
*
* From: Joe Cool <Snoopy at Doghouse> (Say hello to Charlie)
*
*  Now, suppose that the mail file is being routed through an
*  inter-network gateway and the return path ("at doghouse")
*  has to have another host name added.  Clearly, we want to
*  maintain the personal name ("Joe Cool") and the comment
*  (in parens) while inserting the path specification.  By
*  chaining down the path from MBXDML to NODDOWN we get to
*  the TOKEND describing "doghouse".  Now it is a simple
*  matter to allocate a new TOKEND for "at" and one for
*  "Peanut-net" and insert these in the token list to obtain
*  the following result:
*
* from: Joe Cool <Snoopy at Doghouse at Peanut-net> (Say hello...
*
*  Upon output of the new message header, all that has to be
*  done is chain thru the token list and output each token along
*  with assorted padding, etc. to make it look nice.
         SPACE ,
         BLOCKS ,
         SPACE ,
* REGISTER USAGE -
R0 EQU 0 -
R1 EQU 1 -
R2 EQU 2 - WORK REGISTER
R3 EQU 3 - WORK REGISTER
R4 EQU 4 - WORK REGISTER
R5 EQU 5 - NODE BASE
R6 EQU 6 - STACK POINTER
R7 EQU 7 - STACK LENGTH
R8 EQU 8 - CURRENT TOKEN IN TOKEN LIST  (TOKEND BASE)
R9 EQU 9 - CURRENT ADDRESS DESCRIPTOR (MBOX BASE)
R10 EQU 10 - WORK REGISTER
R11 EQU 11 - WORK REGISTER
R12 EQU 12 - BASE REGISTER
R13 EQU 13 - SAVE AREA
R14 EQU 14 -
R15 EQU 15 - RETURN CODE
         PRINT NOGEN
         SPACE 2                                                  UW002
         WXTRN LCLADP                                             UW002
         EJECT ,
ADPARSE  CSECT ,
         USING ADPARSE,R15   TEMPORARY ADDRESSABILITY
         B     EYESKIP       SKIP EYE-CATCHER
MYNAME   DC    CL8'ADPARSE',CL8'&SYSDATE'
EYESKIP  DS    0H
         DROP  R15
         STM   R14,R12,12(R13)     SAVE CALLER'S REGISTERS
         LR    R12,R15       GET PERM ADDRESSABILITY
         USING ADPARSE,R12
         LA    R15,SAVE      GET ADDRESS OF SAVE AREA
         ST    R13,4(R15)    SAVE CALLER'S R13
         ST    R15,8(R13)    CHAIN SAVE AREAS
         LR    R13,R15       POINT AT MY SAVE AREA
         ST    R1,PLIST      SAVE PLIST ADDRESS
         USING PAB,R1        ADDRESS PARMS
         L     R2,@STK       GET STACK POINTER ADDRESS
         L     R6,0(R2)      GET STACK ADDRESS
         L     R3,@LEN       GET STACK LENGTH  ADDRESS
         L     R7,0(R3)      GET STACK LENGTH
         LA    R6,3(R6)      MAKE A FULLWORD ALIGNED STACK
         N     R6,=X'FFFFFFFC'
         LR    R4,R6         COPY IT
         S     R4,0(R2)      COMPARE TO SUPPLIED ADDRESS
         SR    R7,R4         SUBTRACT ANY DIFFERENCE
         BL    NOSPACE       OUT OF SPACE! ARGH!
         ST    R6,0(R2)      ALSO STORE FIXED STACK POINTER
         ST    R7,0(R3)      AND FIXED STACK LENGTH
         DROP  R1            DONE WITH PLIST FOR NOW
         SPACE ,
*--------------------------------------------------------------------
* FIRST CALL TOKENIZER ROUTINE TO TOKENIZE THE INPUT STRING
* NOTE THAT TOKENIZR INPUT PLIST IS A SUBSET OF THIS ROUTINE'S
* PLIST.
*--------------------------------------------------------------------
         L     R1,PLIST      MAKE SURE PLIST IS STILL POINTED TO
         L     R15,=V(LCLADP) [1.20]GIVE USER EXIT A CHANCE TO CHANGE
         LTR   R15,R15       [1.20] THE INPUT STRING
         BZ    NOLCLADP      [1.20]IF NONE, SKIP CALL
         BALR  R14,R15       [1.20]CALL USER EXIT
NOLCLADP EQU   *             [1.20]
         CALL  TOKENIZR,MF=(E,(1))
         LTR   R15,R15       ANY ERRORS?
         BNZ   RET           YES, RETURN
         USING PAB,R1        GET PLIST AGAIN
         L     R2,@STK       GET STACK POINTER
         L     R6,0(R2)      GET UPDATED STACK POINTER
         L     R2,@LEN       GET LENGTH POINTER
         L     R7,0(R2)      GET UPDATED STACK LENGTH
         BL    NOSPACE       OOOPS
         L     R3,@PAR       ADDRESS FOR PARSE LIST
         XC    0(4,R3),0(R3) INITIALLY ZERO THE PARSE LIST
         L     R2,@TOK       ADDRESS OF RETURNED TOKEN LIST
         L     R8,0(R2)      GET FIRST TOKEN ADDRESS INTO R8
         USING TOKEND,R8     ADDRESS THE TOKEN DESCRIPTOR
         CLI   TOKTYPE,X'00' EMPTY LIST?
         BE    DONE          ALL DONE -- NO TOKENS
         ST    R6,0(R3)      THIS IS ADDRESS OF PARSE LIST START
         DROP  R1
         SPACE ,
*--------------------------------------------------------------------
*        NOW PARSE THE TOKENIZED LIST.
*--------------------------------------------------------------------
         MVI   FLAGS,X'00'   CLEAR ALL FLAGS
         XC    PREVADA,PREVADA  ZERO PREV MBOX POINTER
START    EQU   *
         S     R7,=A(MBXSIZ) DECREMENT STACK LENGTH OF MBOX
         BL    NOSPACE       NO SPACE, SORRY
         LR    R9,R6         USE R9 AS BASE OF MBOX
         LA    R6,MBXSIZ(R6) BUMP STACK POINTER
STARTA   EQU   *
         USING MBOX,R9     ADDRESS IT
         XC    0(MBXSIZ,R9),0(R9) INIT TO ALL ZEROS
START0   EQU   *
         CLI   TOKTYPE,TOKLTP START OF A COMMENT?
         BNE   START0A
         BAL   R14,EATCOMM   EAT EM UP
START0A  EQU   *
         CLI   TOKTYPE,X'00' END OF LIST?
         BE    LISTEND       YES, QUIT
         CLI   TOKTYPE,TOKCMA  COMMA?
         BNE   START1        NO, TRY NEXT CHAR
         L     R8,TOKNEXT          POINT AT NEXT ENTRY
         B     START0        MUST BE 'A,,B,' STUFF
START1   EQU   *
         CLI   TOKTYPE,TOKLTB  START OF MACH-ID ?
         BNE   START2        NO, TRY SOMETHING ELSE
         L     R8,TOKNEXT            POINT AT NEXT ENTRY
         OI    FLAGS,MACHID  INDICATE > EXPECTED
START2   EQU   *
         CLI   TOKTYPE,TOKATM  TOKEN IS AN ATOM
         BE    USERNAME      YES, GET USER NAME
         CLI   TOKTYPE,TOKQSTR [1.19]token is a quoted string
         BE    USERNAME      [1.19]yes, get user name
         LA    R15,20        ERROR
         B     RET
         SPACE ,
*--------------------------------------------------------------------
*        PARSE A USER NAME (ONE OR MORE ATOMS)
*--------------------------------------------------------------------
USERNAME EQU   *             GET SOME USERNAME TOKENS
         LR    R5,R6         ALLOCATE AN NODE
         S     R7,=A(NODSIZ) IS THERE ROOM FOR IT?
         BL    NOSPACE       NOPE
         LA    R6,NODSIZ(R6) UPDATE STACK POINTER
         ST    R5,MBXLCL          STORE ADDRESS OF ULST ANCHOR
         XC    MBXDML,MBXDML ZERO IN CASE HOST NEVER SPECIFIED    1.6
         XC    MBXDCNT,MBXDCNT                                      1.6
USERNAM1 EQU   *             MULTIPLE-TOKEN LOOP BACK POINT
         USING NODE,R5     ADDRESS THE DESCRIPTOR
         XC    0(NODSIZ,R5),0(R5) ZERO IT
         CLI   TOKTYPE,X'00' LIST END?
         BE    LISTEND
         CLI   TOKTYPE,TOKLTB START OF MACH-ID?
         BNE   USERNAM2      NO, TRY THE NEXT ONE
         SPACE ,
* 'PERSONAL-NAME <MACHINE-ID...' WAS GIVEN INSTEAD OF 'MACHINE-ID..'
         TM    FLAGS,MACHID  ALREADY IN MACHINE ID?
         BNE   MACHNEST      SORRY, CAN'T NEST THEM!
         L     R8,TOKNEXT            SKIP OVER THE "<"
         OI    FLAGS,MACHID  AND TURN ON '<>' FLAG
         SR    R1,R1         GET ZERO
         L     R1,MBXLCNT    GET # OF WRONG NODES ALLOCATTED
         BCTR  R1,0          -1 FOR 1ST WHICH WE WILL REUSE
         LTR   R1,R1         TEST IF THERE ARE ANY TO RELEASE
         BNH   USENM11       DON'T RELEASE ANY
         SLL   R1,3          MULTIPLY BY 8 TO GET AMOUNT TO RELEASE
         AR    R7,R1         GIVE BACK TO STACK
         SR    R6,R1         MOVE THE POINTER TOO
USENM11  EQU   *
         XC    MBXLCNT,MBXLCNT  SET NAME TOKEN COUNTER BACK TO 0
         L     R5,MBXLCL            GET FIRST NODE AGAIN
         B     USERNAM1      AND GET THE USER NAME
         SPACE ,
MACHNEST EQU   *             NESTED MACHINE-ID BRACKETS ("<FOO <...")
         LA    R15,28        ERROR
         B     RET
USERNAM2 EQU   *
         CLI   TOKTYPE,TOKAT IS IT ATSIGN?
         BNE   USERNAM3      NO, TRY NEXT
USERN21  EQU   *             AT-SIGN AND "AT" CODE
         MVI   TOKTYPE,TOKAT SET IT TO '@' VALUE EVEN IF IT WAS 'AT'
         L     R8,TOKNEXT            SKIP THE ATSIGN
         B     HOSTNAME      AND GO GET HOST NAME
USERNAM3 EQU   *             CHECK FOR KEYWORD "AT"
         CLI   TOKTYPE,TOKATM IS STRING AN ATOM?
         BNE   USERNAMA      [1.19] change to branch to A
         CLC   TOKLEN,=F'2'  LENGTH 2?
         BNE   USERN31       NO, IT CANT BE 'AT'
         L     R4,TOKPTR          GET ADDRESS OF STRING
         CLI   0(R4),C'A'    is it 'A'
         BE    FIX001        yes,  maybe At
         CLI   0(R4),C'a'    is it 'a'
         BNE   USERN31       nope,  can't be at then.
FIX001   EQU   *
         CLI   1(R4),C'T'    is it 'T'
         BE    USERN21       yes,  the token is 'at'
         CLI   1(R4),C't'    or 't'
         BE    USERN21       yes.
*        TM    0(R4),C'a'    IS IT 'a' OR 'A'?
*        BNO   USERN31       NOPE, CAN'T BE "AT" THEN
*        TM    1(R4),C't'    IS IT 't' OR 'T'?
*        BO    USERN21       YES, THIS IS AN '@' EQUIVALENT
         SPACE ,
USERN31  EQU   *             IT'S A USERID TOKEN
         SR    R1,R1         GET ZERO
         L     R1,MBXLCNT    GET USERNAME COUNT
         LA    R1,1(R1)      BUMP IT UP ONE
         ST    R1,MBXLCNT    AND PUT IT BACK
         ST    R8,NODDOWN    SET DOWN POINTER TO TOKEN
         S     R7,=A(NODSIZ) ROOM FOR A NEW NODE?
         BL    NOSPACE       SIGH!
         ST    R6,NODNEXT    SET NEXT POINTER IN CURRENT ONE
         ST    R5,PREVADN    ADDRESS OF PREVIOUS ONE
         LR    R5,R6         AND CHAIN ALONG
         LA    R6,NODSIZ(R6) MOVE THE STACK POINTER
         L     R8,TOKNEXT            GET NEXT TOKEN
         B     USERNAM1      AND DO IT AGAIN....
         SPACE ,
USERNAMA EQU   *             [1.19]
         CLI   TOKTYPE,TOKQSTR [1.19] QSTR == ATOM
         BE    USERN31        [1.19]handle just like atom
USERNAM4 EQU   *             MAYBE IT'S A COMMENT START
         CLI   TOKTYPE,TOKLTP   IS IT A COMMENT?
         BNE   USERNAM5      NO, TRY NEXT ONE
         BAL   R14,EATCOMM   EAT COMMENT
         B     USERNAM1      AND DO IT AGAIN
USERNAM5 EQU   *             MAYBE COMMA: END OF THIS ADDRESS
         CLI   TOKTYPE,TOKCMA  COMMA?
         BNE   USERNAM6      NO, TRY NEXT
USERN51  EQU   *             LOOP BACK HERE FROM '>'
         L     R8,TOKNEXT            POINT AT NEXT TOKEN
         S     R7,=A(MBXSIZ) ALLOCATE A NEW MBOX
         BL    NOSPACE       OUT OF SPACE
         ST    R6,MBXNEXT    SET NEXT POINTER
         ST    R9,PREVADA    SAVE PREV ADA ADDRESS
         LR    R9,R6         CHAIN ALONG
         LA    R6,MBXSIZ(R6) BUMP THE STACK COUNTER
         DROP  R5
         L     R1,PREVADN    CLEAN UP THE PREV. NODE
         USING NODE,R1     ADDRESS IT
         XC    NODNEXT,NODNEXT ZERO THE NEXT POINTER
         DROP  R1
         USING NODE,R5     GET R5 BACK
         B     STARTA        AND DO A NEW ADDRESS
USERNAM6 EQU   *             MAYBE IT'S END OF MACH-ID (">")
         CLI   TOKTYPE,TOKRTB  END OF MACH-ID?
         BNE   USERNAM7      NO, TRY NEXT
         TM    FLAGS,MACHID  WAS THERE A <?
         BO    USERN51       YES, CLEAN UP
         LA    R15,36        NEVER STARTED IT!!
         B     RET
USERNAM7 EQU   *
         LA    R15,40        WHAT ELSE CAN THERE BE?
         B     RET
         SPACE 2
*--------------------------------------------------------------------
*        DONE PARSING USERID. NOW PARSE HOST NAME(S).
*--------------------------------------------------------------------
HOSTNAME EQU   *             GET HOST NAMES
         DROP  R5            DROP NODE FOR A SEC
         L     R1,PREVADN    GET LAST ONE ACTUALLY FILLED
         USING NODE,R1     ADDRESS IT
         XC    NODNEXT,NODNEXT ZERO NEXT POINTER
         DROP  R1
         USING NODE,R5     USE THE EXTRA ONE FOR FIRST HOST NODE
         ST    R5,MBXDML          SET HOST LIST ANCHOR
HOSTNAM1 EQU   *
         XC    0(NODSIZ,R5),0(R5) ZERO THE NODE
         CLI   TOKTYPE,TOKLTP MAYBE THEY MADE A COMMENT
         BNE   HOSTNM11      NOPE, TRY NEXT
         BAL   R14,EATCOMM   EAT UP THE COMMENT
HOSTNM11 EQU   *
         CLI   TOKTYPE,TOKATM BETTER BE AN ATOM
         BNE   HOSTBAD       SORRY...
         CLC   TOKLEN,=F'2'  MAKE SURE IT'S NOT THE ATOM 'AT'
         BNE   HOSTNAM2      SAFE...
         L     R4,TOKPTR          GET ADDRESS OF STRING
         TM    0(R4),C'a'    IS IT 'a' OR 'A'?
         BNO   HOSTNAM2      NO, CAN'T BE START OF 'AT'
         TM    1(R4),C't'    IS IT 't' OR 'T'?
         BO    HOSTBAD       YES, 'AT AT' IS ILLEGAL
         SPACE ,
HOSTNAM2 EQU   *             TOKEN WAS AN ATOM AS HOPED FOR
         ST    R8,NODDOWN    SET THE DOWN POINTER
         SR    R1,R1         GET ZERO
         L     R1,MBXDCNT    GET HOST LIST COUNTER
         LA    R1,1(R1)      INCREMENT BY 1
         ST    R1,MBXDCNT    AND PUT IT BACK
         SPACE ,
* NOW CHECK FOR EITHER AN END TO THE HOST PATH OR ANOTHER ATSIGN
HOSTNM21 EQU   *
         L     R8,TOKNEXT            GET NEXT TOKEN
         CLI   TOKTYPE,TOKLTP COMMENT MAYBE?
         BNE   HOSTNM22      NOPE, TRY SOMETHING ELSE
         BAL   R14,EATCOMM   EAT UP THE COMMENT
HOSTNM22 EQU   *
         CLI   TOKTYPE,X'00' LIST END?
         BNE   HOSTNAM3      NOPE, TRY ANOTHER OPTION
         TM    FLAGS,MACHID  WAS THERE AN OPEN MACH-ID?
         BO    HOSTBAD       THAT'S AN ERROR...
         B     LISTEND       NOW END UP
HOSTNAM3 EQU   *
         CLI   TOKTYPE,TOKCMA          COMMA?
         BNE   HOSTNAM4      NO, CHECK NEXT ONE
         L     R8,TOKNEXT            POINT AT NEXT TOKEN
         S     R7,=A(MBXSIZ) ALLOCATE A NEW MBOX
         BL    NOSPACE       OUT OF SPACE
         ST    R6,MBXNEXT    SET NEXT POINTER
         ST    R9,PREVADA    SAVE PREV MBOX ADDRESS
         LR    R9,R6         CHAIN ALONG
         LA    R6,MBXSIZ(R6) BUMP STACK POINTER
         B     STARTA        AND DO A NEW ADDRESS
HOSTNAM4 EQU   *
         CLI   TOKTYPE,TOKRTB  END OF MACH-ID?
         BNE   HOSTNAM5      NOPE, TRY SOMETHING ELSE
         TM    FLAGS,MACHID  WAS THERE AN OPEN MACHID?
         BNO   HOSTBAD       NOPE, SHOULDN'T HAVE A ">" THEN...
         NI    FLAGS,255-MACHID RESET THE FLAG
         B     HOSTNM21      AND CHECK FOR LIST END OR ...
* WASN'T A LIST END, TRY FOR AN ATSIGN OR "AT"
HOSTNAM5 EQU   *
         CLI   TOKTYPE,TOKAT AT SIGN?
         BNE   HOSTNAM6      TRY SOMETHING ELSE
HOSTNM51 EQU   *
         MVI   TOKTYPE,TOKAT SET CODE TO @, EVEN IF TOKEN WAS 'AT'
         S     R7,=A(NODSIZ) ALLOCATE A NEW NODE
         BL    NOSPACE       OUT OF SPACE
         ST    R6,NODNEXT    SET NEXT POINTER IN CURRENT NODE
         LR    R5,R6         CHAIN TO NEW NODE
         LA    R6,NODSIZ(R6) BUMP STACK POINTER
         B     HOSTNAM1      AND GO DO IT AGAIN
HOSTNAM6 EQU   *             TEST FOR "AT"
         CLI   TOKTYPE,TOKATM IF IT'S AN ATOM, IT BETTER BE "AT"
         BNE   HOSTBAD       CAN'T BE ANYTHING ELSE AT THIS POINT
         CLC   TOKLEN,=F'2'  "AT" IS 2 CHARS
         BNE   HOSTBAD       SORRY. HOST NAMES ARE SINGLE ATOMS.
         L     R4,TOKPTR         GET ADDRESS OF STRING
         TM    0(R4),C'a'    IS IT 'a' OR 'A'?
         BNO   HOSTBAD       SORRY, HOST NAMES ARE SINGLE ATOMS
         TM    0(R4),C't'    IS IT 't' OR 'T'?
         BO    HOSTNM51      IT'S 'AT'. GO DO THE @ CODE NOW
HOSTBAD  EQU   *
         LA    R15,99
         B     RET
         SPACE ,
NOSPACE  EQU   *
         LA    R15,44        INDICATE ERROR
         B     RET
LISTEND  EQU   *
         L     R1,PLIST                GET PLIST ADDRESS
         USING PAB,R1        ADDRESS PLIST
         CLC   MBXLCNT,=F'0' IS THIS A NULL MBOX?
         BNE   LIST1         NO, KEEP ON GOING
         ICM   R9,B'1111',PREVADA GET PREVIOUS MBOX POINTER
         BNZ   LIST1         A PREVIOUS ONE DOES EXIST
         L     R2,@PAR       PARSE LIST POINTER ADDRESS
         XC    0(4,R2),0(R2) ZERO THE ANCHOR IN THIS CASE
LIST1    EQU   *
         LTR   R9,R9               Do we have a MBOX ?          UW003
         BZ    LIST2         ->    No - can't clear pointer      [1.24]
         XC    MBXNEXT,MBXNEXT  KILL ANY DANGLING POINTERS
LIST2    EQU   *             <- here when zero pointer           [1.24]
         L     R2,@STK       GET STACK POINTER ADDRESS
         ST    R6,0(R2)      SET NEW STACK POINTER
         L     R2,@LEN       ADDRESS OF STACK LENGTH
         ST    R7,0(R2)      AND STACK LENGTH
         SPACE
DONE     EQU   *
         SR    R15,R15       ZERO ERRORS
         SPACE ,
RET      EQU       *
         L     R13,4(R13)
         L     R14,12(R13)
         LM    R0,R12,20(R13)
         BR    R14
         SPACE ,
EATCOMM  EQU   *
         L     R8,TOKNEXT            GET NEXT TOKEN
         CLI   TOKTYPE,X'00' UNEXPECTED LIST END?
         BNE   EATCOM2       NOPE, KEEP TRUCKING
         LA    R15,36        ERROR
         B     RET
EATCOM2  EQU   *
         CLI   TOKTYPE,TOKRTP END OF COMMENT?
         BNE   EATCOMM       NOPE, LOOP UNTIL END OF COMMENT
         L     R8,TOKNEXT            POINT PAST COMMENT
         BR    R14
         SPACE ,
         LTORG ,
FLAGS    DS    X             FLAG BYTE
MACHID   EQU   1             MACHINE ID "<>"'S
SAVE     DS    18F
PREVADN  DS    F             PREVIOUS NODE IN USERNAME SECTION
PREVADA  DS    F             PREVIOUS MBOX
PLIST    DS    F
         END   ADPARSE
